Bare arrows have distinct open effect rows
sig f : () -> () -> () fun f()() {} f
stdout : fun : forall a::Row,b::Row.() -a-> () -b-> ()
args : --set=show_quantifiers=true

Bare wild arrows have distinct open effect rows
sig f : () ~> () ~> () fun f()() {} f
stdout : fun : forall a::Row,b::Row.() ~a~> () ~b~> ()
args : --set=show_quantifiers=true

A function cannot use an unrelated open effect row
sig f : (() -> ()) -> () fun f(g) { g() } f
stderr : @.*Type error: The function.*currently allowed effects.*
exit : 1

A handler shares an explicit effect tail with its input computation
sig f : (() {E:()|e}~> ()) -> () {E{_}|e}~> () fun f(g) { fun() { handle(g()) { case <E => res> -> res(()) }}} f
stdout : fun : (() {E:() => ()|a}~> ()) -> () {E{_}|a}~> ()

Anonymous effect tails are independent in a handler signature
sig f : (() {E:()|_}~> ()) -> () { |_}~> () fun f(g) { fun() { handle(g()) { case <E => res> -> res(()) }}} f
stderr : @.*Type error: The non-recursive function definition has return type.*
exit : 1

An operation omitted from a row is unavailable
sig apply : (() {Ask:Int|e}-> Int) -e-> Int fun apply(f) { f() } apply
stderr : @.*Type error: The function.*currently allowed effects.*
exit : 1

Named effect presences can be shared across rows
sig h : (() {Ask:() => Int,Other{p}|e}~> Int) {Ask{q},Other{p}|e}~> Int fun h(f) { handle(f()) { case <Ask => k> -> k(42) } } h
stdout : fun : (() {Ask:() => Int,Other{a}|b}~> Int) {Ask{_},Other{a}|b}~> Int

Flexible effect tail and presence variables
fun(f : (() {Ask{%p},Tell{%}|%}-> Int)) { f() }
stdout : fun : (() {Ask{a},Tell{b}|c}-> Int) {Ask{a},Tell{b}|c}-> Int

The printer keeps an anonymous tail's effect kind
fun() {} : () {|_::Eff}-> ()
stdout : fun : () -_::Eff-> ()

Braced record presence and absence
fun(r : (x{:Int}, y{-}, z{p}|e)) { r.x }
stdout : fun : ((x:Int,y-,z{_}|_)) -> Int

Braced effect presence and absence
fun() { do Ask } : () {Ask{:Int},Tell{-}|e}-> Int
stdout : fun : () {Ask:() => Int,Tell-|_}-> Int

An absent operation cannot be invoked
fun() { do Tell } : () {Ask{:Int},Tell{-}|e}-> Int
stderr : @.*Type error: The inferred type of the expression.*but it is annotated with type.*
exit : 1

Polymorphic nullary operation shorthand
sig f : () {Ask:forall a. a}-> Int fun f(){ do Ask + 0 } f
stdout : fun : () {Ask:forall a.() => a}-> Int

Linear arrows can have open or closed wild rows
(linfun(x) { print(x); x } : (String) ~@ String, linfun(x) { print(x); x } : (String) {}~@ String)
stdout : (fun, fun) : ((String) ~@ String, (String) {}~@ String)

Closed empty effects do not admit wild
fun() { print("hello") } : () {}-> ()
stderr : @.*Type error: The inferred type of the expression.*but it is annotated with type.*
exit : 1

Dot syntax in effect rows is rejected
fun() {} : () {Ask:Int|.}-> ()
stderr : @.*Parse error:.*
exit : 1

Removed effect sugar setting is unknown
()
args : --set=effect_sugar=true
stdout : () : ()
stderr : @.*Unknown setting 'effect_sugar'.*

Removed effect sugar policy setting is unknown
()
args : --set=effect_sugar_policy=open_default
stdout : () : ()
